+# Capture worksheet — fill out before concluding that any audio differs
+
+## Shared target
+- Test scene / map (example `hedge1`):
+- Exact path of reference demo for Alice 2000:
+- SHA-256 of original demo:
+- Exact path of reference demo for Alice 2011:
+- SHA-256 of 2011 demo:
+- Demo length and sound events verified on each system:
+- Same game-data / patch versions (include checksums if possible):
+- Same language/voice-over assets:
+- Same A3D2 provider selected and verified by game diagnostics:
+
+## For each of the FIVE configurations
+
+| Capture | Game build | Demo replay yes/no | A3D provider | Mixer & output settings | WAV start/end |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Alice 2000 / Win10 / Aufake3D | | | | | |
+| Alice 2000 / Wine / Aufake3D | | | | | |
+| Alice 2011 / Win10 / Aufake3D | | | | | |
+| Alice 2011 / Wine / Aufake3D | | | | | |
+| Alice 2000 / Win98SE / real Vortex 2 | | | | | |
+
+Record: Aufake3D DLL SHA-256, HRTF mode (reference/fast), gain, WaveOut polling,
+VorpalFix build, Wine build, Linux backend, Windows audio enhancements and OS
+master volume. For the real card, record exact Aureal driver version, headphone
+mode, native sample rate if known, which line output, ADC model/capture gain,
+and whether the captured signal clipped or had analog noise.
+
+## Listening observations
+- Blind level-matched A/B (yes/no):
+- Source positions and audible event timeline matched (yes/no):
+- Which run sounds most externalized/wide, with a specific 5-second segment:
+- Is front/back positioning different or is only the overall soundstage different?
+- Do any missing sounds/reflections explain the impression?
+- Are the 2000/2011 sound assets actually identical in the selected scene?
+
+The measurements provide evidence, not a single numerical ranking of acoustic fidelity.
